# Predeploy before main

Never merge to `main` while `pnpm predeploy` is red. Same bar for any PR that should land on `main`.

`pnpm predeploy` is the `pipeline` alias. Runs, in order: `pipeline:branch-base` → `typecheck` → `lint` → `test` → `build` → `test:e2e`.

After the change set, run `pnpm predeploy`. Fix until it exits 0. Do not merge. Do not call the branch merge-ready while it is red.

Branch must include latest `origin/main` (`pipeline:branch-base`). Rebase if it does not.

TanStack Start / builder-first repos ship on `check` + `build` instead (`dev-checks.mdc`, `docs/config/tanstack-start.md`) — no `predeploy` there.

CI Analyse + Test unit is not a substitute — local `predeploy` still includes `build`, e2e, and branch-base.
